# Host config deploy manifest — canonical (git) → live (host) path pairs.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# ---------------
# Files under host-compose/ are the canonical source for configuration that
# runs directly on the host (outside Kubernetes). Unlike kustomize/ there is
# no controller reconciling them: the documented deploy step is a manual
# `scp` (docs/phase18-evidence/tombstone-deploy-20260424.md:17). A merged PR
# therefore does NOT mean the live host is running that config.
#
# Faz 24 Bulgu 3-E (2026-07-21) is the incident that motivated this file:
# PR #2711 correctly added the audio-gateway WebSocket `Upgrade`/`Connection`
# forward to host-compose/web-nginx/default.conf and merged green, but nobody
# copied the file to the host. The live edge kept the old config for a full
# day, so the desktop recorder's WS handshake kept failing with
# "Invalid 'Upgrade' header" while git and CI both reported the fix as landed.
#
# scripts/host-config-drift-check.sh reads this manifest and fails when a
# canonical file differs from what is actually deployed, so "merged" can no
# longer be mistaken for "deployed".
#
# CONSTRAINT — no secrets in listed files
# On drift the checker prints a unified diff of both sides into the CI log, so
# only list files that carry no credentials. Config that references a secret by
# path or env var name is fine; config with an inline token, password, or key
# is not. If such a file ever needs drift coverage, compare hashes instead of
# printing the diff.
#
# FORMAT
#   <repo-relative canonical path><TAB><absolute live path on staging-sw>
# Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.

host-compose/web-nginx/default.conf	/srv/platform/web/nginx/default.conf
